<article class="env-lemma" id="094L">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/094L">Lemma <span data-tag="094L">28.2.4</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a quasi-compact and quasi-separated scheme. Then the underlying topological space of $X$ is a spectral space. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Topology, Definition <a href="/tag/08YG" data-tag="08YG">5.23.1</a> we have to check that $X$ is sober, quasi-compact, has a basis of quasi-compact opens, and the intersection of any two quasi-compact opens is quasi-compact. This follows from Schemes, Lemma <a href="/tag/01IS" data-tag="01IS">26.11.1</a> and <a href="/tag/01IT" data-tag="01IT">26.11.2</a> and Lemma <a href="/tag/054D" data-tag="054D">28.2.3</a> above. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>